Building kernelsu-dkms
======================

Build dependencies (debian/control):

    sudo apt install build-essential debhelper dpkg-dev cargo rustc git patch

Then, from the repository root:

    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc          # source + binary package
    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b      # binary package only

The resulting kernelsu-dkms_<version>_<arch>.deb is written to the parent
directory. The package is Architecture: any because it ships the natively
compiled ksuinit binary. Install it with:

    sudo apt install ../kernelsu-dkms_*_$(dpkg --print-architecture).deb

Source format and versioning
----------------------------
The source format is 3.0 (native): this repository *is* the packaging
source, while the KernelSU upstream tree is fetched during the build, so no
orig.tar.gz is needed. A native version must not contain a Debian revision,
so debian/changelog uses the upstream-style version directly. For
packaging-only changes, bump with a suffix instead of a "-1" revision:

    dch -v 3.3.0+7+gfde078c9+deb1 "Packaging fix"

Where the upstream sources come from
------------------------------------
debian/rules (target prepare-source) shallow-clones
https://github.com/supechicken/KernelSU.git, branch waydroid-experimental,
into ./kernelsu. It then applies 0001-Patch-Kbuild-for-dkms.patch so that
kernel/Kbuild stops probing for a git repository, builds userspace/ksuinit
with cargo, and copies kernel/ into the DKMS tree. An existing ./kernelsu
checkout and the ./.deb-build cargo cache are reused across builds (both
are excluded from the source tarball). "debian/rules clean" only removes
debhelper's staging directory; delete ./kernelsu and ./.deb-build manually
for a from-scratch rebuild.

The generated DKMS tree is placed in debian/kernelsu-dkms/usr/src/ and is
excluded from the source tarball by debian/source/options.

Build knobs (pass as environment variables to dpkg-buildpackage, because
debian/rules declares them with ?=):

    KSU_REPO          upstream git URL
    KSU_BRANCH        branch to clone (default waydroid-experimental)
    KSU_COMMIT        pin the checkout to a commit hash
    KSU_SRC           path to a pre-existing checkout (default ./kernelsu)
    KSU_GIT_VERSION   value substituted into dkms.conf; setting it skips the
                      "git fetch --unshallow" history lookup
    KSU_UNSHALLOW=0   do not unshallow the clone (faster; set
                      KSU_GIT_VERSION explicitly in that case)

For an offline build, prepare ./kernelsu and a populated cargo cache (or a
vendored crate directory) first, then for example:

    KSU_GIT_VERSION=12345 KSU_UNSHALLOW=0 CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true \
      dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

Updating the version
--------------------
updater.sh reads the latest upstream release, writes a new
debian/changelog entry with dch and verifies the build. The old
makepkg/.SRCINFO/PKGBUILD workflow is no longer used for Debian builds;
those files are kept only for reference.
